# EA3-only kernel config, on top of board/ea/common/linux/common.fragment.
# The EA3 is the same computer as the EA1 (CE5310, same eMMC layout and
# bootloader); two things differ: no Wi-Fi, and reachability is wired-only.
# The wireless stack is off by family default (this board does not list the
# `wifi` feature). e1000 is in the common fragment; its -EIO at probe is SOLVED
# below (fake-PHY patch).

# ── BCM53125 managed switch (DSA/b53) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Kernel side + full explanation live in ea/common/features/switch/, pulled in by
# the 'switch' entry in ohc.features. Port 1's DSA bring-up is still unproven on
# hardware; S40net falls back to the master if DSA does not attach.
#
# Measured on a live EA3 without DSA (plain e1000): only the primary jack (switch
# port 2) reaches the network — port 1 links and receives (MIB Rx climbs, TxOctets
# stays 0) but the stock switch config never forwards it to the CPU port. That is
# the argument FOR the DSA work: without a switch driver the second RJ45 is unusable.

# --- kernel command line (EA3) ---
# `nocrs` IS REQUIRED here, same as the EA1 (tested both ways). The ACPI _CRS on
# this SoC declares only a 48 KB TPM window for the root bus and never mentions
# the 0xc0000000-0xdfffffff space where every on-SoC device lives; without nocrs
# the bus-01 bridge window "can't claim" and the kernel hangs at ~1.02s before
# userspace. With nocrs the kernel derives windows from E820 and boots.
#
# e1000 -EIO at probe: SOLVED. The CE5300 GbE has no PHY on the MDIO bus (MAC
# wired back-to-back to the BCM53125), so the ce4100 PHY autodetect found nothing
# and e1000_probe() returned a bare -EIO. patches/linux/0003-e1000-ce5300-fake-phy.patch
# ports Control4's "fake PHY" mode. PROVEN on hardware 2026-08-26 (eth0 Link Up).
#
# RAM reclaim -- PROVEN ON HARDWARE 2026-08-31: MemTotal 190688 -> 1807608 kB
# (9.5x), ACPI clean, boots to userspace. CEFDK's e820 hands Linux only
# [0x00100000-0x0c7fffff] (200 MB) and marks [0x0c800000-0x7fffffff] (1.8 GB)
# "device reserved" — the Intel CE media carve-out, real idle DRAM openHC never
# loads; reclaiming it is what lets WPE WebKit run (needs >1 GB).
#
# It has to be memmap=exactmap: the additive form is silently dropped (e820
# sanitisation resolves overlaps toward the HIGHER type, so "reserved" beats added
# "RAM"). Every entry below is load-bearing:
#   68K@0            low memory, reproduced faithfully
#   60K#0x11000      THE ACPI TABLES — claiming them as RAM gives
#                    AE_NO_ACPI_TABLES and the box boots to 706 MB then hangs
#   512K@0x20000     rest of low memory
#   255M@1M          CEFDK's 200 MB region MERGED with the gap above it, to 256M
#   1536M@0x10000000 the reclaim, ending at 0x70000000 — 128 MB margin before the
#                    0x78000000 stop line, far below the framebuffer at 0x7fc00000
#
# Do NOT widen past 0x78000000: the framebuffer must not become System RAM or
# ce5300-fb refuses to probe (display gone), and the region just under it holds
# CEFDK structures the box needs to reboot. This crosses the 32-bit lowmem
# boundary (~934 MB highmem; userspace unaffected).
#
# EA-3 v2 ONLY. These figures describe THIS board's map; another CEFDK split needs
# its own numbers, and a memmap past the end of real DRAM is unrecoverable remotely.
# pci=routeirq enables the CE5300 UART interrupt link (LUAR/GSI 38) for the IO-MCU
# on ttyS1 — see board/ea/common/linux/common.fragment.
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=ttyS0,115200 earlyprintk=serial,ttyS0,115200 pci=realloc,nocrs,routeirq memmap=exactmap memmap=68K@0 memmap=60K#0x11000 memmap=512K@0x20000 memmap=255M@1M memmap=1536M@0x10000000"

# eMMC storage (sdhci-pci + ext4) comes from ea/common/features/emmc/linux.fragment
# via the 'emmc' entry in board/ea/ea3-v2/ohc.features.
